From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msi: Keep the resolved directory property when a SelectionTree control binds it.

AI-assisted (Claude, Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Browse indirection still follows the selected feature (the SOLIDWORKS
installer's feature tree overwrote INSTALLDIR). Temporary L3-only
exception by the maintainer's decision of 2026-11-10.

Header added on 2026-11-11, before winum-11.20-1 (the patch body is
unchanged). Problem, cause, Windows behaviour and validation:
docs/patches/msi-selection-tree-directory-property.md.

--- a/dlls/msi/dialog.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/dialog.c
@@ -634,7 +634,11 @@
     else if ( !wcscmp( attribute, L"Property" ) )
     {
         MSIFEATURE *feature = seltree_get_selected_feature( ctrl );
-        if (feature) dialog_set_property( dialog->package, ctrl->property, feature->Directory );
+        /* A real directory property contains a resolved path, not another
+         * directory identifier. Keep it intact when the feature changes.
+         * Browse indirection properties still track the selected directory. */
+        if (feature && ctrl->property && !msi_get_loaded_folder( dialog->package, ctrl->property ))
+            dialog_set_property( dialog->package, ctrl->property, feature->Directory );
     }
     else if ( !wcscmp( attribute, L"SelectionPath" ) )
     {
